  "question": {
    "text": "A crystal is made up of metal ions&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#39;</mo></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#39;</mo></math>&nbsp;and oxide ions. Oxide ions form a ccp lattice structure. The cation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#39;</mo></math>&nbsp;occupies&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></math>&nbsp;of octahedral voids and the cation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#39;</mo></math>&nbsp;occupies&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>%</mo></math>&nbsp;of tetrahedral voids of oxide lattice. The oxidation numbers of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#39;</mo></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#39;</mo></math>&nbsp;are respectively :",
